  "mechanism": [
    "Existing users row locked before account checks and token changes; managed user refreshed after waiting.",
    "Refresh lookup resolves owner ID, locks user, then re-reads and locks exact supplied token before verification and rotation.",
    "Logout locks sorted distinct access/refresh owners before either mutation; preserves independently supplied exact-token behavior."
  ],
  "preservedBehavior": [
    "One current refresh token per user; concurrent logins succeed and latest serialized login supersedes prior refresh.",
    "A consumed refresh token yields 401 instead of producing multiple replacement pairs.",
    "Logout of an old refresh never revokes a newer replacement token by user ID.",
    "Logout is token-specific; other access JWTs remain valid until expiry or explicit invalidation.",
    "Wrong-password five-attempt temporary lock policy is unchanged; concurrent attempts now persist correctly."
  ],
  "iterations": [
    "Before implementation, three focused real-PostgreSQL regressions failed: first simultaneous login, same-token refresh and duplicate access-only logout.",
    "Expired-token test fixture uses JDBC Timestamp because PostgreSQL driver cannot infer java.time.Instant parameter type. No product change was needed for that fixture."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Scope is local disposable PostgreSQL/H2 and existing auth unit/controller checks; parent orchestrates HTTP/browser and full Maven validation.",
    "Zalo live third-party OAuth was not exercised; existing mocked Zalo unit behavior passed.",
    "No global logout, cookies, SSO or CSRF contract was introduced."
  ]
